(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2609161013-fleet-cleanup-kbb-rewrite-mangling")
  (:adr/title "fleet cleanup 2026-09-16: UNLANDED survey drained to a ledger landing, four preserved branches, one retired stash — and the stash exposed a kbb-cutover rewrite that mangled a local function on aiueos main")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-16")
  (:adr/related (vector "ADR-2609160849" "ADR-2609112000" "ADR-2608136000" "ADR-2609061800" "ADR-2607211600"))
  (:adr/context
  "Owner asked for `git cleanup conflict` (skill git-cleanup-conflict) after the closing of ADR-2609160849, then `do it` on the resume point that ADR's cleanup left (verify and land aiueos PR #348). Both correct SSoT files were read in full first (manifest/cleanup-workflow.md 57 KB, cleanup-workflow.edn 84 KB, 29 sections).

  Inventory (local scans only; no fleet-wide west update, per the 2026-09-09 revision):
  - superproject: main == origin/main, stash 0, open PR 0, tracked changes 0, untracked 132 (orgs/ 116 classified by the orphan audit; the rest is owner material, listed under Not touched).
  - scripts/checkout-staleness.cljk: 4,556 checkouts, dirty 87, ahead 15 — every ahead is parked on a side branch, ahead-on-default-branch = 0; 6 checkouts on a named non-default branch.
  - scripts/cleanup.cljk --unlanded: UNLANDED 78 child repos, completed (48/200 PR round-trips, no truncation, 3 ls-remote checks, no false unpushed).
  - scripts/west-orphan-audit.cljk: blocking 0, true-orphan-git 0, renamed-unverified 0, renamed-upstream 96 (rename residue, never re-register), personal 21, worktree-scratch 3, true-orphan-nongit 2. --blocking exit 0 (not 2) is the completion gate and it held before and after.
  - scripts/cleanup-land.cljk dry-run over 4,491 checkouts (70 with a file .git): :additive 0 repos — the rank-1 untracked counts that looked alarming (app-aozora 1,076, net-kotobase 287, kami-app-modeler 12, app-hyakka 2) were all build output, .cpcache / clj-kondo cache, >2 MB or credential-shaped and the gates dropped every one; :review 4 repos of 1–2 tracked files each.
  - scripts/worktree-retire.cljk dry-run (min-age 3 d, stopped after ~30 min at 139 rows because git status on the sparse superproject worktrees takes >7 min each under load): keep 92, UNVERIFIED 27 (git status exit 124 = timeout, not a verdict), PRUNE 18, RETIRE 1.

  What the :review candidates actually were (read before opening anything): amu cljk-origin.edn = a regenerated registry on a checkout 24 behind — and origin/main's own registry lists four files its tree no longer has (scripts/native-route-parity.cljk, scripts/test-definition-cid-parity.cljk, src/kotoba/compiler/nbb/module_lock.cljk, src/kotoba/compiler/nbb/project_files.cljk); control-plane-legal-candidate = a rebuilt minified authn-worker.js plus .pyc; apps-gftdcojp = submodule content; kotoba-lang site/dist html = 1 line of a build artefact; loop-consumability evidence/consumability.ledger.edn = +822 lines, 0 deletions, an append-only ledger the loop writes into the shared checkout without committing (:ledger-blocker).

  The stash finding. orgs/kotoba-lang/aiueos held one stash (b360c25a, 2026-09-15 21:54, message claiming '0 novel blobs vs kotoba-lang/main'). Measured instead of believed: base daffd45 is 592 commits behind main; of 182 changed files 68 blobs exist nowhere on main; of those, 21 are .clj/.cljs whose .cljk twins exist on main (the 2026-09-11 rename) and 47 differ from main only by the kbb cutover rewriting (nbb → kbb --backend sci, clojure.string → kotoba.lang.text) plus lines main later moved past; splitting each residual line into 'already at the stash base' vs 'novel' left 12 novel lines in 4 files, and the 4 in os/aiueos/kotoba/aiueos/lib/sha256_stream.kotoba were the ORIGINAL text: main has `(kbb -M:blk j)` where the stash has `(bb blk j)`. `bb` is defined in that file — `(defn bb [blk i] (kernel-load-u8 blk 64 i))` — and the kbb cutover commit de57a31 (731 rewrites in 199 files) matched it as a babashka invocation. The reader still accepts the file, so nothing flagged it. `git grep '(kbb -M:[a-z]' origin/main` in that repo: only this file (a docstring in build-k16-pure-native.cljk and one provenance.edn line are legitimate text). Verdict for the stash itself: superseded — every stash-only line was either at the base or overtaken by main, and the one real difference is the regression above.")
  (:adr/decision
  "Landed (all merged server-side, none by force):
  - network-awai/loop-consumability PR #8 → main e61897b2: the 45 ledger lines main lacked (777 of the 822 were already landed by PR #7 the night before). Verified before merge: origin/main's ledger + these 45 lines is byte-identical to the shared checkout's file; all 2,940 lines read as EDN maps with distinct :tick/at. Disposition :merge by the preservation rule (0 deleted lines, base current). Archive: the checkout's .git/stash-archive-2026-09-16/consumability-ledger-45-lines.{patch,txt}.
  - kotoba-lang/industry #13 #14 #15 and kotoba-lang/comfyui #16: local-only branches (verified absent from the remote by ls-remote) pushed to preserve them and opened as draft PRs by cleanup-land --apply --branches; each carries a comment with the measurement (industry: the ISIC 4653 / 4662 / 2410+2811 registrations have 0 occurrences on main — genuinely un-landed, base 800+ commits stale, and the branch edits test/kotoba/industry_test.clj which main renamed to .cljk) and disposition needs-review. Four other local-only branches sit in archived repos (kqe, open-banking, com-etzhayyim-gov_municipality, manimani) and were left, per the 2026-08-14 owner decision.
  - kotoba-lang/aiueos PR #348 → main 352c3851: the four `(bb blk …)` calls restored. Verified both directions with the repo's own admission runner (os/aiueos/scripts/verify-admissions.cljk on the kbb engine, node --stack-size=60000, ulimit -s 65520, classpath = the :verify-admissions alias closure resolved from ~/.gitlibs — amu ca869d79, kotoba-sema e42b74ef, osaho 08bdab8b overriding amu's kotoba-kir, 29 libs, none missing — plus ../text/src and ../org-ietf-ssh/src): origin/main's file → `FAILED: operation has no admitted lowering {:form (kbb -M:blk j) :kotoba.error/code :kotoba.error/subset-reject}` exit 1; the fix → `CONTRACT :aiueos.sha256-stream/v1 vectors=5 steps=34 traps=0 memory=4` exit 0. Provenance: os/aiueos/kotoba/provenance.edn records :source-sha256 c3d5f9c1… for the module; the fixed file hashes to exactly that (as does the pre-cutover file de57a31^), main's file hashed to 4e8c4520… — main contradicted its own provenance. The repo's `CLJC contract tests` Actions check is red on the PR AND on main 6724ef48 with the same kotoba.security.adoption/verify! (adoption.clj:215) failure — pre-existing, not required, not caused here. The stash was then archived (.git/stash-archive-2026-09-16/b360c25a…patch + .files + index.txt) and dropped by re-resolved index.
  - west pins advanced by scripts/west-pin-put.cljk (single-entry, server-side, ahead/behind checked by API): aiueos 6724ef48 → 352c3851 (root 568cedd4), loop-consumability 2523e0f2 → e61897b2 (root 44803f63). The aiueos shared checkout was aligned with `west update --fetch smart aiueos` (first attempt aligned it to the OLD pin because the local west.yml had not fast-forwarded yet — the FF was blocked by a stale index.lock; see below).
  - cloud-itonami/open-banking: one worktree registration whose directory was gone, pruned.
  - superproject .git/index.lock removed twice (08:49 and 09:52 creations; each 0 bytes, no holder in lsof, no git write process, >8 min old) so the shared checkout could fast-forward. Some other session's git is dying mid-operation and leaving the lock; the lock is not work, so removing it destroys nothing, but the pattern is recorded because the third time should be investigated rather than swept.

  Not landed, by decision (each named so the next pass does not re-derive it):
  - No :review PR for amu / control-plane-legal-candidate / apps-gftdcojp / kotoba-lang — generated or built artefacts, not WIP. amu's stale registry on main is a real (small) finding: regenerate cljk-origin.edn on main with the generator, do not commit a copy from a stale checkout.
  - orgs/network-awai/net-kotobase: slug collision with control-plane-legal-candidate (two copies of net-kotobase/control-plane); the tool leaves the 30 candidates to a human.
  - aozora-yoro-ui dirty=667 is the deletion of tracked .shadow-cljs cache; deletions are never applied. Fix is on main: .gitignore via the ignore-rule-gate procedure, then git rm --cached.
  - app-itonami dirty=18 = svelte/ deleted mid-migration; deletions never applied.
  - app-kotoba-cloud's 3 stashes (newest 04:20 'wip') belong to a session that was active hours earlier; untouched.
  - Six worktree paths the retire script called 'directory gone' exist with 2–16 entries and only the .git pointer missing (/private/tmp/svelte-wave-{manako,cyber-drill,shigotoba}, /private/tmp/itonami-isic-research, /private/tmp/claude-501/aiueos-build, /private/tmp/app-coverage-wt); possibly uncommitted work, not pruned.
  - The loop that writes consumability.ledger.edn appended 2 more lines within an hour of the landing: it does not land its own lines (the :ledger-blocker durable fix — land-new-ledger-lines! in ~/.itonami/bmc-tick.cljs — exists for bmc, not for this loop). The same 45-line shape will recur every day until that loop calls scripts/ledger-land.cljk.
  - The remaining UNLANDED ladder (≈40 repos with pushed-no-PR branches; branch farms of 546 / 476 / 262 / 211 branches) is the standing work of the hermes branch-drain / pr-drain profiles, not of a hand pass.

  Verification fixed: every measurement above is a command in this record or in the PR bodies/comments; no test suite claims a pass it did not execute (the JVM parity test was not run and says so in #348).")
  (:adr/body
  "Remaining gaps, by priority:
  1. The kbb cutover rewrite (de57a31 in aiueos, and the same wave in 198 other files there and in every repo the cutover touched) can mangle any local symbol named bb / nbb / clj / clojure into a `kbb -M:…` form; the reader does not object. Fleet check: `git grep -n -E '\\(kbb -M:[a-z]' <default>` per repo, excluding docs/scripts where the text is prose; the detector verify-kbb-rewrite-path-literals is registered and has never run (SessionStart says so) — this is exactly its job, so run it once and read what it prints. Provenance :source-sha256 comparisons (as in aiueos) catch the compiled-object cases mechanically.
  2. loop-consumability's tick needs the same land-new-ledger-lines! call bmc-tick has; until then the ledger re-accumulates daily in the shared checkout.
  3. amu cljk-origin.edn on main lists 4 files that do not exist; regenerate on main.
  4. industry #13/#14/#15: replay only the registry.edn entries onto a branch from current main, port the test assertions into the .cljk test, run a suite that executes >0 tests, then close these with the successor linked. comfyui #16: strict containment check first (added lines on main AND no removed line still on main), then replay or close superseded.
  5. Superproject index.lock left behind by another session (twice today, 0 bytes, no holder): if it happens again, find the dying process (ps for git write ops right after the lock appears) before removing.
  6. Repo hygiene on main for aozora-yoro-ui (.shadow-cljs tracked) and the net-kotobase duplicate checkout.
  7. Carried from ADR-2609160849: hermes auxiliary.compression routes to api.kotoba.cloud with claude-sonnet-5 (owner still not answered), and no guard stops a non-Claude-Code deploy of kotoba-cloud-control-plane from a stale checkout.

  Resume point (next agent, no history needed):
  - cd orgs/kotoba-lang/aiueos && git fetch origin && git grep -n -E '\\(kbb -M:[a-z]' origin/main -- ':!*.md'   (expect only build-k16-pure-native.cljk's docstring and provenance.edn's prose; anything in a .kotoba/.cljk form is a gap-1 hit)
  - kbb --backend sci scripts/cleanup.cljk --unlanded   (the 78-row ladder; untracked rows are build output unless cleanup-land's dry-run says :additive > 0)
  - grep -n 'ledger-land\\|land-new-ledger' orgs/network-awai/loop-consumability/scripts/*.cljk ~/.itonami/bmc-tick.cljs   (gap 2: the loop has none of it)

  Owner WIP preserved, not touched: everything under Not landed above; superproject untracked owner files (cookies.json — credential-shaped, 865 B at the repo root, worth moving —, ck.txt, b300-glm53/, docs/kotoba-cloud-*.md, docs/design/, .tmp-line-research/, .worktrees/, .hermes/plans/*, orgs/personal/litigation/* 6 files); the five other-session superproject worktrees (.gftd/worktrees/social-catalog-maint, Codex 2026-09-12/13 root-* ×4: landed but 3–4 days old, kept); app-kotoba-cloud's shared checkout and its /private/tmp/akc-* worktrees; no stash created; no branch of anyone else moved; my own worktrees (3) and branches removed, remote branches for the four preserved-branch PRs kept.")
))
